  "releaseNotes094": "Your own courses are in the course list under +: untick one to hide it from the row at the top (it is kept), the pencil opens it for editing.\nAn own course carries a hand-tool mark in the row at the top instead of its host's face.\nAn achievement still ahead: its host now holds it, a grey medal with a padlock.\nAbout: tap Goro, he has a few new poses.\nHome screen: before the first workout of the day your host has a word for you (each host its own, a new one every time you open the app or tap it), and below are your next goals (the next rank, the nearest achievement, an open challenge you can start right there) and the branches of the course.\nAfter it, the home screen shows your latest workouts and what grew today: more reps, a set, less rest, a new stage.\nThe arrow on the workout button unfolds today's plan, with Goro showing every exercise.\nGoro's animations wherever an exercise is named: the path of a branch, the Courses tab, the builders, saved workouts, the history, the rest before the next exercise.",
  "releaseNotes095": "Friends are gone: without a server they could only swap a QR code once, and that was it. The app no longer needs the camera or Bluetooth.\nYour name: your host greets you by it on the home screen, and the profile and the end of a workout show it. Change it in Settings → Profile.\nFour new branches outside the courses: Strong Back, Glutes, Arms & Shoulders and Cardio — 22 exercises, each with Goro’s animation. Add them to your own course: Courses → + → Create your own course.",
  "releaseNotes0911": "Take your progress with you: Settings → Your data → “Save progress to a file”, then on the other device “Add progress from a file”. It joins what is there: the workouts, SP, streak, stages and achievements of both, nothing is lost. From the web version to the app, or to a new phone.\nIf both devices had a workout on the same day, the one with more SP stays the first of the day and the other counts as a bonus workout.\nAfter adding a progress file, its workouts can go to Apple Health or Health Connect as well: those at a time when a workout is already there are skipped.\nOn Android, workouts now really reach Health Connect: until now they did not get there.",
  "releaseNotes0910": "Want TreniDay as an Android app? In the web version on an Android phone, About invites you to become a tester: Google Play lets a new app in after 12 people have tested it for two weeks.\nThe Apple Health permission requests speak your language.\nOn Android, the privacy policy link in Health Connect opens the policy.",
  "releaseNotes099": "CaliDay is now TreniDay: a new name, the same Goro and all your progress.\nThe web version has moved to pupptmstr.github.io/treniday/app — open it in the same browser and your progress is there.",
  "releaseNotes098": "The web version on iPhone now plays every workout sound — the ticks, the start of a hold, switch sides, the end of a rest — not only the ones that follow a tap.\nTreniDay has a website: pupptmstr.github.io/treniday — what the app is about, in four languages.",
  "releaseNotes097": "New home-screen widgets with Goro: Today (the day's plan, the week and the streak, in three sizes), Goro (his face follows your day: he sleeps at night, frowns when your streak is at risk, cheers after a workout), Streak and Rank. Goro takes a new pose every day.\nOn iPhone there are widgets for the lock screen too: the streak, the way to the next rank and today's plan.\nA tap on a widget opens its place: the workout, Home, the calendar or the profile.",
  "releaseNotes096": "You can train your own courses only: in the course list under + untick every built-in course — one ticked course of any kind is enough.\nAn achievement opens across the whole width of the screen, not just as wide as its text.\nNew workout sounds, a cue for every moment: get ready, the hold starts, halfway, switch sides, set done, the next exercise, Skala’s challenge, the end. They play over your music instead of stopping it. Settings → Sounds: all, key only or off.",
  "releaseNotes093": "Make your own course: in the Courses tab tap + and pick branches from any course, choose its host and give it a name.\nA branch of your own: pick exercises and put them in order, each one becomes a stage. Reps, sets, rests and the challenges are set by the app, as in every branch.\nUnder the bell, the latest updates come first; the whole history of TreniDay, version by version, is folded below them.",
  "releaseHistory01": "The first version: short daily workouts, SP points, streaks, reminders and a first-run setup.\nFive skills: push-ups, core, pull-ups, legs and balance; the workout takes turns between them day by day.\nThe path of a skill: every stage on one screen, and a challenge to move on early.\nAchievements, extra workouts on the same day and a dark theme.\nRussian and English.\nGoro shows every push-up stage in an animation.",
  "releaseHistory02": "Sound and vibration during a workout.\nThe workout history.\nA new home screen with three tabs at the bottom.\nStreak freezes: one missed day no longer breaks the streak.\nThe About screen.",
  "releaseHistory03": "A home screen widget with your streak and SP.\nApple Health and Health Connect: workouts are saved there if you want.",
  "releaseHistory04": "Friends: add each other with a QR code or find each other nearby over Bluetooth, and compare ranks, SP and streaks.\nThe first-run setup asks your name.",
  "releaseHistory05": "Courses: Calisthenics and the new Healthy Body, with posture and neck skills.\nA flexibility and mobility skill.\nExtra workouts bring two exercises from a new supplementary set.\nGoro's animations for the core, pull-up and leg stages.",
  "releaseHistory06": "The exercise library: every exercise, with search and filters.\nTap the streak, the rank or the freezes in the profile to see what they mean.",
  "releaseHistory07": "Your own workouts: pick exercises and save them as a routine, or start a quick one by focus.\nAnimations for the balance stages.\nThe privacy policy and the terms of use.",
  "releaseHistory08": "The stats on the home screen open the calendar, the history and the ranks; a workout calendar.\nA rank slips after long breaks and comes back with training.\nTreniDay in the browser: the web version.\nAnimations for every exercise of the first courses.\nTimed holds start by themselves after a short countdown; a hold on one side runs on both.\nWorkouts are Short, Standard or Full, with an estimate of the time that learns your pace.\n“What's new” under the bell in the profile; German and Spanish.\nEvery skill moves on once a day, in any workout.\nA new course, Evening Stretch, and a host for every course.",
  "releaseHistory09": "New courses: Morning Routine with Aurora the lark, and Yoga with Miso the cat.\nHosts present the achievements of their course; shorter holds on each side.\nEvery exercise has an animation.\nYour own courses: built-in branches and branches of your own, made of exercises in your order.\nFriends removed; your host greets you by name.\nFour branches outside the courses: back, glutes, arms and shoulders, cardio.\nA sound for every moment of a workout, over your music.\nHome-screen widgets with Goro: Today, Goro, Streak and Rank; on iPhone on the lock screen too.\nA new name: CaliDay is now TreniDay.\nYour progress moves with a file: to a new phone, or from the web version to the app."
}